{
  "_format": "tt-strategy/v2",
  "_readme": {
    "about": "Tradetron strategy export. Edit and re-import via the ASB Import button.",
    "logic": "To change a condition's logic, edit its 'conditionJson' (the AST).",
    "do_not": "Do not add '*_id' foreign keys back.",
    "patch_notes": "v4 architecture: 4 independent Sets (Chop-CE, Chop-PE, Bullish, Bearish), each with its own Entry + Exit (no Repair Once anywhere, per Tradetron's documented Repair-Once-counter-reset limitation). Direction filter uses native Kaufman Adaptive MA slope (offset 0 vs -1), not DMI. Stop distance is dynamically scaled by native Kaufman Efficiency indicator instead of a fixed point value: stop = wide_points - (ER * (wide_points - tight_points)). Strike selection uses Find Strike (Fx formula, searching by LTP/premium), not a 'Premium' dropdown - that field does not exist in Tradetron's Strike Selection Type list.",
    "UNVERIFIED_1": "Kaufman Adaptive MA's exact input parameters in your Tradetron version are unconfirmed - it may take a single period, or the full 3-parameter ER-period/fast-SC/slow-SC set like the original KAMA(10,3,30). Check what fields appear when you select the keyword and adjust 'period' placeholders below accordingly.",
    "UNVERIFIED_2": "The nested Math Operation formula used for the ER-scaled stop distance (wide - ER*(wide-tight)) is written here as a formula sketch. Tradetron's actual nested-Fx UI may require building this differently (e.g. via multiple chained Math Operation keywords). Rebuild this specific formula by hand in the Exit condition's Fx box rather than trusting this JSON's structure verbatim.",
    "UNVERIFIED_3": "All 'kid' numeric IDs in conditionJson/strikeJson below (including for Kaufman Adaptive MA, Kaufman Efficiency indicator, Find Strike, Math Operation, Get Runtime Number) are placeholders, not confirmed values from a live Tradetron export. Rebuild every condition and Fx formula via the UI dropdowns before relying on this file - do not import and run as-is without checking each condition in the builder."
  },
